1️⃣ Conformed Dimension

What
A conformed dimension is a shared dimension that is used consistently across multiple fact tables and data marts.

Why

Ensures consistent reporting
Enables cross-functional analysis
Avoids duplicate dimensions

Where Used

Across:
Multiple fact tables
Enterprise Data Warehouses

Healthcare Example

Dim_Date, Dim_Patient, Dim_Provider

Used by:
Fact_Encounters
Fact_Claims
Fact_Lab_Results

Same Patient_SK means the same patient everywhere.

Scenario

In our healthcare EDW, I worked with conformed Patient and Date dimensions so clinical, financial, and operational reports all aligned on the same patient definitions.
-------------------------
2️⃣ Role-Playing Dimension
What

A role-playing dimension is a single physical dimension that plays multiple roles in a fact table.

Why
Avoids duplicate dimensions
Simplifies maintenance

Where Used
When the same dimension applies in multiple contexts.

Healthcare Example

Dim_Date used as:

Admission Date
Discharge Date
Billing Date

Scenario

I used the Date dimension as a role-playing dimension in Fact_Encounter to analyze length of stay and billing timelines.
--------------------
3️⃣ Degenerated Dimension
What

A degenerated dimension is a dimension attribute stored directly in the fact table, without a separate dimension table.

Why
No additional descriptive attributes
Improves performance
Simplifies design

Where Used
Transactional identifiers.

Healthcare Example
Claim Number
Encounter Number
Invoice Number

Scenario

In Fact_Claims, the Claim_Number was stored as a degenerated dimension because it had no descriptive attributes.
-----------------------------
4️⃣ Junk Dimension
What

A junk dimension groups low-cardinality, unrelated flags and indicators into a single dimension table.

Why
Avoids many tiny dimensions
Cleaner schema
Better performance

Where Used
Flags like Yes/No, status indicators.

Healthcare Example

Dim_Visit_Flags
Emergency Visit (Y/N)
Readmission (Y/N)
Telehealth (Y/N)

Scenario

I created a junk dimension table to store multiple visit flags instead of adding many columns to the fact table.
